WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:04.211
If you need any indication of the direction
movies are going in this fall, well, Lego

00:00:04.220 --> 00:00:07.120
Batman said it best: Darkness, no parents.

00:00:07.330 --> 00:00:11.300
From a Girl with the Dragon Tattoo sequel
to a long-awaited first look at The Conjuring's

00:00:11.310 --> 00:00:16.099
spinoff-slash-prequel The Nun, June is promising
a Halloween season that'll have you cowering

00:00:16.099 --> 00:00:17.099
under the covers.

00:00:17.099 --> 00:00:19.669
That said, it's not all doom and gloom on
the docket.

00:00:19.669 --> 00:00:24.240
June also brought us trailers for Ralph Breaks
the Internet, the Peter Jackson-produced Mortal

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:27.769
Engines, and the Transformers spinoff Bumblebee,
to name a few.

00:00:27.769 --> 00:00:32.570
In fact, we're looking at incredible trailers
for movies as far out as 2019, which means

00:00:32.570 --> 00:00:33.860
there are a lot to run through.

00:00:33.860 --> 00:00:38.520
Here are all the trailers from June 2018 for
movies that are sure to blow you away.

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:39.840
Siberia

00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:44.740
Keanu Reeves is front and center in the first
trailer for Siberia, a crime thriller about

00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:48.520
a sketchy diamond smuggler who heads to Russia
to look for his missing partner.

00:00:48.580 --> 00:00:52.780
There, he discovers that his partner was trying
to cheat some terrifyingly serious Russian

00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:53.280
mobsters.

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:57.260
Will he be able to make it out of Siberia
in one piece, or will he find himself on the

00:00:57.260 --> 00:00:58.960
wrong side of Russian justice?

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:02.220
Find out when Siberia lands in theaters on
July 13th.

00:01:02.780 --> 00:01:03.520
Poor Boy

00:01:04.260 --> 00:01:06.920
To be honest, Poor Boy doesn't look like an
instant classic.

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:11.060
The story of two hustling brothers who concoct
a scheme to finally get out of their nowhere

00:01:11.060 --> 00:01:16.740
town, the film hit a few festivals in 2016
and then disappeared until it secured a 2018

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:17.240
release date.

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:22.140
The highlight of the trailer has to be Michael
Shannon in rodeo clown makeup delivering slow,

00:01:22.149 --> 00:01:25.229
existential quotes while he takes long drags
on his cigarette.

00:01:25.229 --> 00:01:27.780
Hopefully that won't be the only reason to
see Poor Boy.

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:31.299
But even if it is, well, there are worse ways
to spend an afternoon.

00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:32.700
Look for it on July 13th.

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:34.860
Robin Williams: Come Inside My Mind

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:37.920
What can you say about Robin Williams that
hasn't been said before?

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:39.680
"I do a great impression of a hot dog"

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:48.079
He entertained decades of fans, and now, HBO
is releasing a documentary about Williams'

00:01:48.079 --> 00:01:50.959
life to twist the faucet on those tear ducts
one more time.

00:01:50.959 --> 00:01:55.259
With a wealth of behind-the-scenes footage,
photographs from his childhood, and interviews

00:01:55.259 --> 00:01:59.770
with Williams' friends and family, Robin Williams:
Come Inside My Mind looks like an intimate

00:01:59.770 --> 00:02:01.729
glimpse into the life of the legendary comic.

00:02:01.729 --> 00:02:05.740
"There you are, you've become a reformed alcoholic,
you've got a steaming glass of Perrier going,

00:02:05.740 --> 00:02:07.140
'I feel so much better about myself!'"

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:09.940
Take a look when it premieres on HBO on July
16th.

00:02:10.680 --> 00:02:11.340
Alpha

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:16.140
The story of a dog and his prehistoric boy,
Alpha is having no trouble tugging at viewers'

00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:17.540
heartstrings with its trailers.

00:02:17.620 --> 00:02:21.720
Full of sweeping music and touching moments,
Alpha's trailers bill it as a movie about

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:23.160
the domestication of dogs.

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:26.180
Think of it as the gritty origin story of
your mom's Corgi.

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:30.780
And okay, that may not seem like gripping
cinema at first glance, but Alpha might just

00:02:30.780 --> 00:02:32.570
pull it off through spectacle alone.

00:02:32.570 --> 00:02:37.390
The trailers reveal rich cinematography filled
with gorgeous landscapes and soaring aerial

00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:37.880
shots.

00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:41.700
Throw in a story about a sad wolf, and you've
got your hands on cinematic gold.

00:02:41.880 --> 00:02:43.480
Look for Alpha on August 17th.

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:45.400
The Little Stranger

00:02:46.360 --> 00:02:51.610
With 2015's Room, director Lenny Abrahamson
made a unique, gut wrenching movie about a

00:02:51.610 --> 00:02:54.100
mother who would go to any lengths to protect
her son.

00:02:54.100 --> 00:02:58.690
The first trailer for his upcoming The Little
Stranger reveals another subtle, nerve-jarring

00:02:58.690 --> 00:03:01.040
ride, this time with a supernatural twist.

00:03:01.270 --> 00:03:05.380
The story centers on a small-town doctor,
played by Domhnall Gleeson, who's called out

00:03:05.390 --> 00:03:07.750
to an old estate to fix up a sick maid.

00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:11.770
It isn't long before the old house begins
revealing disturbing secrets, suggesting a

00:03:11.770 --> 00:03:13.200
supernatural presence.

00:03:13.340 --> 00:03:18.420
The Little Stranger is based on the 2009 gothic
novel of the same name, and arrives in theaters

00:03:18.420 --> 00:03:19.940
on August 31st.

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:21.120
The Nun

00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:25.660
The creepy, evil nun Valak made her first
appearance in The Conjuring 2, and The Nun

00:03:25.670 --> 00:03:29.620
will serve as something of an origin story
for the demon, with the main story centered

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:33.500
on a Romanian priest and a young nun who are
investigating what happened to a nun in an

00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:34.100
old church.

00:03:34.360 --> 00:03:37.880
It looks like a delightfully eerie popcorn
movie to check out this fall.

00:03:37.880 --> 00:03:39.940
The Nun hits theaters on September 7th.

00:03:40.600 --> 00:03:41.280
Mandy

00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:45.980
Here's what we figured out from the trailer
for Mandy: If losing your mind was a color,

00:03:45.980 --> 00:03:48.400
it'd be Nic Cage in neon pink with a homemade
battle axe.

00:03:49.340 --> 00:03:50.760
"So what you huntin'?"

00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:53.840
"Crazy evil!"

00:03:54.020 --> 00:03:57.940
The story of a man and a girl living in the
woods who get targeted by a sadistic biker

00:03:57.940 --> 00:04:02.510
cult, Mandy is somewhere between an acid trip
and a horror movie, the perfect platform for

00:04:02.510 --> 00:04:05.920
Nic Cage to let loose with whatever it is
that Nic Cage lets loose with.

00:04:05.940 --> 00:04:09.260
Take a look when Mandy barrels into theaters
on September 14th.

00:04:09.860 --> 00:04:10.900
The Old Man and the Gun

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:15.700
Robert Redford headlines this upcoming crime
film as an old man who knocks over banks by

00:04:15.700 --> 00:04:17.310
flashing a gun and a smile.

00:04:17.310 --> 00:04:21.370
The Old Man and the Gun is based on the real
life of Forrest Tucker, a career criminal

00:04:21.370 --> 00:04:23.740
who escaped from prison nearly 20 times.

00:04:23.890 --> 00:04:28.080
The events of the film follow Tucker as an
elderly man who's still pulling heists, enchanting

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:32.460
the bank workers with his gentlemanly smile
even as he makes off with thousands in cash.

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:33.580
"He had a gun."

00:04:33.580 --> 00:04:34.540
"You saw it?"

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:36.660
"Well, he was also sort of a gentleman."

00:04:36.980 --> 00:04:40.260
Robert Redford is perfectly cast to play a
suave, elderly criminal.

00:04:40.500 --> 00:04:44.900
And with Casey Affleck, Sissy Spacek, and
Danny Glover co-starring, The Old Man and

00:04:44.900 --> 00:04:46.760
the Gun looks like a guaranteed winner.

00:04:46.840 --> 00:04:48.820
Look for it on September 28th.

00:04:49.480 --> 00:04:51.040
Bad Times at the El Royale

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:55.980
When seven strangers show up at a seedy hotel
near Lake Tahoe, the meeting kicks off a fateful

00:04:55.980 --> 00:04:57.760
night where nothing is what it seems.

00:04:58.020 --> 00:05:01.040
As the hours in the hotel wear on, each of
them reveals a dark secret.

00:05:01.900 --> 00:05:03.480
"I'm not really a priest."

00:05:03.480 --> 00:05:05.620
"Yeah, no s---."

00:05:05.780 --> 00:05:09.600
Written and directed by Drew Goddard, who
also helmed the genre-twisting Cabin in the

00:05:09.601 --> 00:05:13.310
Woods, Bad Times at the El Royale is a tour
de force of star power.

00:05:13.310 --> 00:05:17.960
Jeff Bridges, Chris Hemsworth, Dakota Johnson,
and Jon Hamm headline the film, and the brief

00:05:17.960 --> 00:05:21.300
trailer hits all the right beats without giving
away any plot twists.

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:24.780
Check in to the El Royale when the movie lands
in theaters on October 12th.

00:05:25.520 --> 00:05:26.360
First Man

00:05:26.940 --> 00:05:30.890
Directed by the Oscar-winning director of
La La Land, First Man centers on a young Neil

00:05:30.890 --> 00:05:34.620
Armstrong during the lead-up to the Apollo
11 mission to land on the moon.

00:05:34.920 --> 00:05:38.590
Of course, it's safe to say that we know how
the story will end, but the dramatized version

00:05:38.590 --> 00:05:42.780
of the momentous event coupled with Ryan Gosling's
portrayal of Armstrong should be enough to

00:05:42.780 --> 00:05:44.760
keep audiences on the edge of their seats.

00:05:44.760 --> 00:05:46.980
Look for First Man to land on October 12th.

00:05:48.040 --> 00:05:48.880
Serenity

00:05:49.500 --> 00:05:53.740
Matthew McConaughey stars in this upcoming
thriller as a quiet fishing boat captain who

00:05:53.740 --> 00:05:56.900
gets an unexpected visit from his ex-wife,
played by Anne Hathaway.

00:05:57.100 --> 00:06:00.840
She has a simple request: Take her current
husband out on the water and leave him for

00:06:00.840 --> 00:06:01.340
the sharks.

00:06:01.480 --> 00:06:05.560
After that, the trailer grinds into gear,
throwing out tantalizing glimpses of the story

00:06:05.560 --> 00:06:08.740
while the slow tick of a fishing reel drives
up the tension.

00:06:08.940 --> 00:06:12.770
If the movie is anywhere near as good as the
trailer, Serenity looks like a sure win to

00:06:12.770 --> 00:06:14.360
look forward to later this year.

00:06:14.600 --> 00:06:16.840
Check it out when it reaches theaters on October
19th.

00:06:17.660 --> 00:06:19.060
Ralph Breaks the Internet

00:06:19.300 --> 00:06:23.370
The story of an arcade villain who decides
that he wants to become a hero, 2012's Wreck-It

00:06:23.370 --> 00:06:27.460
Ralph is both an awesome love letter to video
games and a heartfelt adventure tale.

00:06:27.460 --> 00:06:29.100
"And where you coming from?"

00:06:29.100 --> 00:06:30.160
"Ahhh, Pac-Man!"

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:31.850
"You bring any fruit with ya?"

00:06:31.850 --> 00:06:33.320
"No, no fruit!"

00:06:33.320 --> 00:06:34.020
"Okay then."

00:06:34.140 --> 00:06:37.680
If the trailer for the sequel is any indication,
it's heading in the same direction.

00:06:37.880 --> 00:06:42.139
After a worryingly Emoji Movie-esque opening
that sees Ralph and Vanellope travel to the

00:06:42.139 --> 00:06:46.550
internet and gaze out over a sprawling city
of product placement, the trailer finds its

00:06:46.550 --> 00:06:47.040
stride.

00:06:47.040 --> 00:06:50.840
Vanellope ends up in a room full of Disney
princesses, they escape from stormtroopers,

00:06:50.840 --> 00:06:52.600
and it all looks like a lot of fun.

00:06:52.980 --> 00:06:55.800
Check out Ralph Breaks the Internet on November
21st.

00:06:56.060 --> 00:06:57.980
"Shouldn't it be Ralph Wrecks the Internet?"

00:06:57.980 --> 00:07:00.200
"Yes, since he is Wreck It Ralph?"

00:07:00.200 --> 00:07:02.160
"Uh yeah, but, break the internet?

00:07:02.300 --> 00:07:02.940
It's like, a thing."

00:07:03.500 --> 00:07:04.880
The Girl in the Spider's Web

00:07:05.640 --> 00:07:09.780
Sony seems to have a plan for their adaptations
of the Millennium book series, even if nobody

00:07:09.780 --> 00:07:10.920
else can figure it out.

00:07:10.960 --> 00:07:15.460
Trailing David Fincher's 2011 The Girl with
the Dragon Tattoo and a complete, critically

00:07:15.460 --> 00:07:20.080
acclaimed trilogy of Swedish film adaptations,
Sony is replacing the entire cast and moving

00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:22.700
straight to the fourth novel, The Girl in
the Spider's Web.

00:07:22.940 --> 00:07:25.640
To be fair though, this new take looks like
it's in good hands.

00:07:25.760 --> 00:07:29.780
Don't Breathe's Fede Alvarez is directing,
with Golden Globe winner Claire Foy stepping

00:07:29.780 --> 00:07:32.260
in as hacker vigilante Lisbeth Salander.

00:07:32.260 --> 00:07:34.340
Look for it in theaters on November 9th.

00:07:35.140 --> 00:07:35.880
Creed II

00:07:36.300 --> 00:07:39.260
Michael B. Jordan is returning to the ring
this year in Creed II.

00:07:39.380 --> 00:07:43.180
The trailer sees Creed training harder than
ever while balancing his family life.

00:07:43.320 --> 00:07:48.030
It all ends with a tantalizing glimpse of
Ivan Drago's son, promising an epic, emotional

00:07:48.030 --> 00:07:48.520
fight.

00:07:48.520 --> 00:07:53.020
The first Creed film became a surprise hit
when it was released in 2015, resulting in

00:07:53.020 --> 00:07:57.860
an Oscar nomination for Best Supporting Actor
for Sylvester Stallone and a major box office

00:07:57.860 --> 00:07:58.360
take.

00:07:58.480 --> 00:08:01.100
Creed II looks like it's following in the
same footsteps.

00:08:01.100 --> 00:08:02.640
Look for it on November 21st.

00:08:03.420 --> 00:08:04.560
Welcome to Marwen

00:08:05.100 --> 00:08:09.650
Steve Carell stars in Welcome to Marwen as
Mark Hogancamp, an artist who lost his ability

00:08:09.650 --> 00:08:12.060
to draw after he was beaten by neo-Nazis.

00:08:12.240 --> 00:08:16.520
Through extensive, detailed miniature models,
Mark channels his imagination into a new form

00:08:16.520 --> 00:08:17.700
of art: dolls.

00:08:17.860 --> 00:08:21.720
"Now I am making your silver pants blue."

00:08:22.320 --> 00:08:26.480
And sometimes, his imagination takes him straight
into the stories of the dolls themselves.

00:08:26.490 --> 00:08:30.880
Welcome to Marwen looks like one of the most
unique movies to hit theaters in 2018.

00:08:30.880 --> 00:08:33.040
Take a look when it premieres on November
21st.

00:08:33.540 --> 00:08:34.540
Mortal Engines

00:08:35.280 --> 00:08:38.760
The Oscar-winning screenwriting team behind
The Lord of the Rings is taking on another

00:08:38.760 --> 00:08:43.560
epic adaptation this December with Mortal
Engines, a post-apocalyptic tale about wheeled

00:08:43.560 --> 00:08:46.740
cities that rove around the land preying on
weaker cities.

00:08:46.740 --> 00:08:50.940
The story centers on a young woman named Hester
Shaw, who becomes a fugitive from the rolling

00:08:50.940 --> 00:08:54.900
city of London after she attempts to assassinate
a powerful man named Valentine.

00:08:55.060 --> 00:08:58.750
The trailer sets up the premise beautifully
while leaving the main meat of the story for

00:08:58.750 --> 00:08:59.800
the movie itself.

00:08:59.980 --> 00:09:02.220
Look for Mortal Engines on December 14th.

00:09:02.880 --> 00:09:03.580
Bumblebee

00:09:04.280 --> 00:09:09.000
Eleven years and five movies after kids first
fell in love with HD robot toys, the Transformers

00:09:09.000 --> 00:09:10.720
franchise is getting back to its roots.

00:09:11.029 --> 00:09:15.380
Bumblebee sees the magical beginnings of the
yellow car alien known as, well, Bumblebee,

00:09:15.380 --> 00:09:18.630
back when he was just a humble VW Bug in a
dusty scrapyard.

00:09:18.630 --> 00:09:23.050
Hailee Steinfeld stars as the human girl who
discovers him, kicking off a new adventure

00:09:23.050 --> 00:09:27.460
that sees the unlikely duo on the run from
the evil government and eviler robots.

00:09:27.460 --> 00:09:30.920
Sort of like the first movie, if all the people
were replaced with different people.

00:09:31.080 --> 00:09:35.980
Take a look when Bumblebee transforms and
rolls into theaters in December 2018.

00:09:36.240 --> 00:09:38.340
The LEGO Movie 2: The Second Part

00:09:38.860 --> 00:09:42.900
Bricksburg is in dire straits in the first
trailer for The LEGO Movie 2, which sees the

00:09:42.900 --> 00:09:46.560
town of LEGO people transformed into a post-apocalyptic
wasteland.

00:09:46.820 --> 00:09:49.700
But desolate ruins and sewer babies aren't
enough to get Emmet down.

00:09:49.860 --> 00:09:53.620
He's still the cheerful, naive guy he always
was, Master Builder or not.

00:09:53.780 --> 00:09:58.160
The LEGO Movie 2: The Second Part is scheduled
to hit theaters in February 2019.

00:09:59.080 --> 00:09:59.620
Dumbo

00:10:00.300 --> 00:10:04.430
Continuing their ongoing march of live-action
remakes, Disney released their first trailer

00:10:04.430 --> 00:10:05.640
for Dumbo this June.

00:10:05.840 --> 00:10:09.550
The journey of a little circus elephant who
gets picked on until he learns how to fly,

00:10:09.550 --> 00:10:12.560
it's definitely a story that's been enchanting
kids for generations.

00:10:12.700 --> 00:10:16.470
The new trailer doesn't go into much of the
story, instead focusing on the essence of

00:10:16.470 --> 00:10:19.630
the tale, which is nothing short of pure childhood
magic.

00:10:19.630 --> 00:10:21.700
Look for it in theaters in March 2019.

00:10:22.140 --> 00:10:23.120
Thanks for watching!

00:10:23.130 --> 00:10:25.709
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:10:25.709 --> 00:10:27.900
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

